  "title": "Why it's called Poison Canyon",
  "text": "Salt Wells Canyon, commonly called Poison Canyon, lies on Highway 178 about 10 miles out of Ridgecrest. It earned the name because the small stream at its west end contains toxic levels of several minerals. Rocks in the canyon known as the Fish Head Rocks were originally called the Whale Heads. They were originally painted sometime in the late 1930s or early 1940s.",
