      "publisher": "Roadside America",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-03",
      "quote": "In Salt Wells Canyon, Commonly called 'Poison Canyon' are the 'Fish Head Rocks,' originally called 'Whale Heads.' ... Highway 178, about 10 miles out of Ridgecrest ... The rocks were originally painted sometime in the late 1930s or early 1940s. ... the small stream at its west end contains naturally occurring arsenic, selenium and other minerals at toxic levels."
